Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(diaspora): restore Curated heritage catalog stat as a
 minimal caption
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Globe-first redesign dropped the entire old stats grid, including the
Curated heritage catalog metric that scripts/diaspora-final-wiring-contract.test.mjs
still asserts must be visible on the dashboard. The metric was still being
fetched into state (stats.heritage_collections) but never rendered.

Restores it as a single small caption line next to the existing My Family /
Legacy strip, consistent with the same 'keep the function, drop the
marketing panel' treatment already applied to family_tree_people on this
page — not a return to the old crowded dashboard.

Verified against a fresh postgis/postgis:16-3.4 database, replicating every
step of the Typecheck + Tests CI job plus Release Validation:
 - pnpm run typecheck (clean)
 - backend tests (@workspace/api-server)
 - pnpm --filter @workspace/db run migrate (144 migrations, incl. 0063)
 - civic seed regression
 - all 10 files under scripts/run-repo-diaspora-contracts.sh (was 1 failing)
 - nia-service tests
 - App/AI boundary test + boundary check script
 - eslint . --max-warnings 0
 - release-validate.js + test:production-gate
